#{\footnote # making_pif}${\footnote $ Making a PIF}K{\footnote K Making a PIF}+{\footnote + procedures:010}
\pard\sb120\sa120\li120{\b\fs28 Making a PIF}\par
\pard\li120\sa60\sb60{\b To make a PIF}\par
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa60 1.\tab Type the program's file name, with its path.\par
2.\tab Type a window title, optional parameters and the start-up directory.\par
3.\tab Set the memory and options the program needs.\par
4.\tab Save the PIF, usually with the program's name and the extension .PIF.\par
\pard\li120\sa120 A program run from Program Manager or File Manager uses its PIF when one has its name; a ? in Optional Parameters asks for them when it starts.\par
\page
#{\footnote # reserving_keys}${\footnote $ Reserving Shortcut Keys}K{\footnote K Reserving Shortcut Keys}+{\footnote + procedures:020}
\pard\sb120\sa120\li120{\b\fs28 Reserving Shortcut Keys}\par
\pard\li120\sa120 Reserve Shortcut Keys passes the checked Alt+Tab, Alt+Esc or Ctrl+Esc combinations to the DOS program. Prevent Program Switch disables switching with all three.\par
\page
